Commits on Feb 20, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ class.c: allocate ROM table wrappers per mrb_state ](/mruby/mruby/commit/71cb3c2e3af6cf9f131c4b91186821bbe0fd40d4 \"class.c: allocate ROM table wrappers per mrb_state\n\nROM method tables used static mrb_mt_tbl variables shared\nacross the process. The next pointer in each wrapper was\nmutated by mrb_mt_init_rom\\(\\), causing cross-state\ncontamination when multiple mrb_state instances existed.\n\nAllocate mrb_mt_tbl wrappers per-state via mrb_malloc\\(\\).\nThe const mrb_mt_entry\\[\\] arrays remain static and shared.\nWrappers are tracked in mrb->rom_mt and freed at mrb_close\\(\\).\n\nRemove MRB_MT_ROM_TAB macro; add MRB_MT_INIT_ROM macro that\nauto-computes size and calls the new mrb_mt_init_rom\\(\\).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\")\n\nShow description for 71cb3c2 \n\n[ matz ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=matz)\n\nand \n\n[ claude ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=claude)\n\ncommitted  on Feb 20 \n\nVerified \n\n[ 71cb3c2  ](/mruby/mruby/commit/71cb3c2e3af6cf9f131c4b91186821bbe0fd40d4) View commit details \n\nCopy full SHA for 71cb3c2 \n\n[ ](/mruby/mruby/blob/71cb3c2e3af6cf9f131c4b91186821bbe0fd40d4/src/range.c) View code at this point  [ ](/mruby/mruby/tree/71cb3c2e3af6cf9f131c4b91186821bbe0fd40d4) Browse repository at this point \n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ proc.h: unify method flag layout; eliminate aspec shifting ](/mruby/mruby/commit/4a097525df94764871941d3e0567cf1974809f1d \"proc.h: unify method flag layout; eliminate aspec shifting\n\nMove MRB_METHOD_FUNC_FL to bit 24 and visibility flags to\nbits 25-26 so that MRB_ARGS_*\\(\\) values \\(bits 0-23\\) can be\nstored directly without shifting. This makes MRB_MT_PRIVATE\nand MRB_METHOD_PRIVATE_FL the same value, eliminating the\ndual-constant confusion and simplifying the MRB_MT_ENTRY\\(\\)\nmacro to a single OR operation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\")\n\nShow description for 4a09752 \n\n[ matz ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=matz)\n\nand \n\n[ claude ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=claude)\n\ncommitted  on Feb 20 \n\nVerified \n\n[ 4a09752  ](/mruby/mruby/commit/4a097525df94764871941d3e0567cf1974809f1d) View commit details \n\nCopy full SHA for 4a09752 \n\n[ ](/mruby/mruby/blob/4a097525df94764871941d3e0567cf1974809f1d/src/range.c) View code at this point  [ ](/mruby/mruby/tree/4a097525df94764871941d3e0567cf1974809f1d) Browse repository at this point \n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ class.c: store aspec in ROM method table entries ](/mruby/mruby/commit/483c155a41e86e8f904702f69acc93fd58059284 \"class.c: store aspec in ROM method table entries\n\nRestore MRB_ARGS_* argument specs and ISO section comments to all\n709 ROM method table entries. The aspec is encoded in bits 4-27 of\nthe flags field; MRB_MT_NOARG is now auto-derived from aspec==0.\n\nAdd MRB_MT_ENTRY_PRIVATE\\(\\) macro for private methods \\(53 entries\\)\nand MRB_MT_ASPEC\\(\\) accessor for extracting aspec from flags.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\")\n\nShow description for 483c155 \n\n[ matz ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=matz)\n\nand \n\n[ claude ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=claude)\n\ncommitted  on Feb 20 \n\nVerified \n\n[ 483c155  ](/mruby/mruby/commit/483c155a41e86e8f904702f69acc93fd58059284) View commit details \n\nCopy full SHA for 483c155 \n\n[ ](/mruby/mruby/blob/483c155a41e86e8f904702f69acc93fd58059284/src/range.c) View code at this point  [ ](/mruby/mruby/tree/483c155a41e86e8f904702f69acc93fd58059284) Browse repository at this point \n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ class.c: auto-set MRB_MT_FUNC in MRB_MT_ENTRY macro ](/mruby/mruby/commit/8adba34bd9667db4715fbf6cbe44ce21a297778a \"class.c: auto-set MRB_MT_FUNC in MRB_MT_ENTRY macro\n\nSince ROM table entries are always C functions, have the\nMRB_MT_ENTRY\\(\\) macro set MRB_MT_FUNC automatically. This\nsimplifies entry definitions across all 32 source files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\")\n\nShow description for 8adba34 \n\n[ matz ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=matz)\n\nand \n\n[ claude ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=claude)\n\ncommitted  on Feb 20 \n\nVerified \n\n[ 8adba34  ](/mruby/mruby/commit/8adba34bd9667db4715fbf6cbe44ce21a297778a) View commit details \n\nCopy full SHA for 8adba34 \n\n[ ](/mruby/mruby/blob/8adba34bd9667db4715fbf6cbe44ce21a297778a/src/range.c) View code at this point  [ ](/mruby/mruby/tree/8adba34bd9667db4715fbf6cbe44ce21a297778a) Browse repository at this point \n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Feb 19, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ class.c: use linear search for method tables; make ROM entries const ](/mruby/mruby/commit/0fab7030282971c345969b8d4e383b8764b6a361 \"class.c: use linear search for method tables; make ROM entries const\n\nReplace binary search with linear scan in mt_get\\(\\), mt_put\\(\\),\nmt_del\\(\\), mt_chain_has\\(\\), and mrb_mt_foreach\\(\\). The method cache\nmakes repeated lookups O\\(1\\), so linear scan on cache misses is\nacceptable.\n\nThis removes the sorting requirement, allowing ROM entry arrays\nto be declared const. On embedded systems, const static data\nresides in flash/ROM instead of RAM, saving ~8.4KB for ~700\nmethod entries on 32-bit MCUs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\")\n\nShow description for 0fab703 \n\n[ matz ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=matz)\n\nand \n\n[ claude ](/mruby/mruby/commits?author=claude)\n\ncommitted  on Feb 19 \n\nVerified \n\n[ 0fab703  ](/mruby/mruby/commit/0fab7030282971c345969b8d4e383b8764b6a361) View commit details \n\nCopy full SHA for 0fab703 \n\n[ ](/mruby/mruby/blob/0fab7030282971c345969b8d4e383b8764b6a361/src/range.c) View code at this point  [ ](/mruby/mruby/tree/0fab7030282971c345969b8d4e383b8764b6a361) Browse repository at this point \n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ class.c: refactor ROM method tables to array-of-structs layout ](/mruby/mruby/commit/bde2202100a4ec5324793f90e71667af068db1a1 \"class.c: refactor ROM method tables to array-of-structs layout\n\nRep